IMPORT `uc2-sch10-capital-disregards`
IMPORT `uc2-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer (uc2-seat.l4): the questions of a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, put as that person
-- would put them, with the facts that person would state. At least one case for every question, and the boundary of every threshold
-- the text states; cases that the text does not answer are asserted as "nothing" (not covered).
--
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text of the Regulations (../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt) and written beside the
-- case; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each argument is given in the order of the question's inputs.


§ `Part 6, Chapter 1 -- Capital (regulations 46 to 50)`

-- reg 46. The sort of a sum: a personal possession first; instalments next; then regular payments; then capital.
-- a car I own is a personal possession
#ASSERT `How is a sum I have treated for universal credit` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `not treated as capital because it is a personal possession`
-- instalments: 10,000 outstanding + 7,000 other = 17,000, over 16,000, so each instalment is income
#ASSERT `How is a sum I have treated for universal credit` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10000 7000 FALSE EQUALS `treated as income`
-- instalments: 9,000 + 7,000 = 16,000 is not over 16,000, so it is capital that counts
#ASSERT `How is a sum I have treated for universal credit` FALSE FALSE TRUE 9000 7000 FALSE EQUALS `capital that is taken into account`
-- a sum paid regularly by reference to a period is income
#ASSERT `How is a sum I have treated for universal credit` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS `treated as income`
-- capital that a rule leaves out
#ASSERT `How is a sum I have treated for universal credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 3000 TRUE EQUALS `capital that is disregarded`
-- ordinary capital
#ASSERT `How is a sum I have treated for universal credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 3000 FALSE EQUALS `capital that is taken into account`
-- reg 46(4): over 16,000 pounds, not at 16,000.
#ASSERT `Is each instalment of capital I am paid by instalments treated as income` 10000 7000
-- exactly 16,000 does not exceed 16,000
#ASSERT NOT (`Is each instalment of capital I am paid by instalments treated as income` 9000 7000)
-- reg 47: equal shares unless the evidence shows otherwise; a share is rounded to the penny.
-- two owners: half of 60,000
#ASSERT `How much of a capital asset I own jointly with others is mine` 60000 2 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 30000
-- three owners: a third of 60,000
#ASSERT `How much of a capital asset I own jointly with others is mine` 60000 3 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 20000
-- the evidence shows a quarter share
#ASSERT `How much of a capital asset I own jointly with others is mine` 60000 2 TRUE 0.25 EQUALS JUST 15000
-- a third of 1,000 to the penny
#ASSERT `How much of a capital asset I own jointly with others is mine` 1000 3 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 333.33
-- NOT COVERED: nobody owns it, so there is no equal share to compute
#ASSERT `How much of a capital asset I own jointly with others is mine` 60000 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- reg 48(2): the 6 months of Schedule 10 is never shorter than 6 once extended.
#ASSERT `How many months does the 6-month period in Schedule 10 last for me` FALSE 0 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `How many months does the 6-month period in Schedule 10 last for me` TRUE 9 EQUALS 9
-- a figure under 6 is not an extension
#ASSERT `How many months does the 6-month period in Schedule 10 last for me` TRUE 4 EQUALS 6
-- reg 49: market value, less 10% if there would be selling expenses, less encumbrances; abroad; conversion charge first (fork F-CAP2).
#ASSERT `What is my capital asset worth for universal credit` 100000 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 100000
-- 100,000 less 10,000 (10%) less 20,000 owed
#ASSERT `What is my capital asset worth for universal credit` 100000 FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE 20000 FALSE 0 EQUALS 70000
-- abroad and not transferable: what it would raise here
#ASSERT `What is my capital asset worth for universal credit` 100000 TRUE TRUE 80000 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 80000
-- abroad but transferable: the value there
#ASSERT `What is my capital asset worth for universal credit` 100000 TRUE FALSE 80000 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 100000
-- less a 200 conversion charge
#ASSERT `What is my capital asset worth for universal credit` 10000 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 TRUE 200 EQUALS 9800
-- 10,000 - 200 = 9,800; less 10% = 980; less 1,000 owed = 7,820
#ASSERT `What is my capital asset worth for universal credit` 10000 FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE 1000 TRUE 200 EQUALS 7820
-- reg 50(1), (2).
-- gave it away to get universal credit
#ASSERT `Am I treated as still having capital that I got rid of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- paid a debt
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as still having capital that I got rid of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- bought goods, reasonably
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as still having capital that I got rid of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- bought goods, but not reasonably
#ASSERT `Am I treated as still having capital that I got rid of` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- not to get universal credit
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as still having capital that I got rid of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `How much capital that I got rid of am I treated as still having` 8000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 8000
-- paid a debt: none
#ASSERT `How much capital that I got rid of am I treated as still having` 8000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- reg 50(3): over 16,000, less the award it would have been; 6,000 to 16,000, less the yield of reg 72; 6,000 or below, no reduction in the text.
#ASSERT `How much notional capital do I have after an assessment period` 20000 900 EQUALS 19100
-- yield: (10,000 - 6,000)/250 = 16 steps x 4.35 = 69.60; 10,000 - 69.60
#ASSERT `How much notional capital do I have after an assessment period` 10000 0 EQUALS 9930.4
-- 16,000 is not over 16,000: yield 40 steps x 4.35 = 174; 16,000 - 174
#ASSERT `How much notional capital do I have after an assessment period` 16000 0 EQUALS 15826
-- at 6,000 the text provides no reduction
#ASSERT `How much notional capital do I have after an assessment period` 6000 0 EQUALS 6000

§ `Part 6, Chapter 2 -- Earned income (regulations 52 to 64)`

-- reg 52: args = job, trade, from work I do, work done for pay, charity or volunteer, paid only expenses, treated as earned income by the Chapter
-- pay from a job
#ASSERT `Is the income I receive earned income` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- profit from my trade
#ASSERT `Is the income I receive earned income` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- other paid work
#ASSERT `Is the income I receive earned income` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- a volunteer paid only expenses is not in paid work (reg 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the income I receive earned income` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- a volunteer paid more than expenses is in paid work
#ASSERT `Is the income I receive earned income` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- unpaid work
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the income I receive earned income` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- treated as earned income by this Chapter
#ASSERT `Is the income I receive earned income` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- none of them
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the income I receive earned income` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- reg 53(2): a body (or the Secretary of State) consulting you about services or functions, and consulting you in your capacity as an affected person; or the carer of such a person.
-- consulted by a health body as a user
#ASSERT `Am I participating as a service user` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- consulted by a research body as a user
#ASSERT `Am I participating as a service user` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- consulted by the body but not in your capacity as an affected person
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I participating as a service user` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- consulted by the Secretary of State as a person affected by the functions
#ASSERT `Am I participating as a service user` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- the carer of a person consulted
#ASSERT `Am I participating as a service user` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I participating as a service user` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- reg 54: an estimate is allowed in two cases.
#ASSERT `May a decision about my earned income be based on an estimate` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `May a decision about my earned income be based on an estimate` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May a decision about my earned income be based on an estimate` FALSE FALSE)
-- estimate allowed and made
#ASSERT `On which amount is my earned income for an assessment period based` TRUE FALSE 500 TRUE 650 EQUALS 650
-- estimate not allowed: the actual amount
#ASSERT `On which amount is my earned income for an assessment period based` FALSE FALSE 500 TRUE 650 EQUALS 500
-- estimate allowed but none made
#ASSERT `On which amount is my earned income for an assessment period based` TRUE FALSE 500 FALSE 0 EQUALS 500
-- unreported income: the estimate
#ASSERT `On which amount is my earned income for an assessment period based` FALSE TRUE 500 TRUE 700 EQUALS 700
-- reg 54A: args = earlier award, day it ended, first day of the new claim, not entitled since, income in the last month, nil UC threshold, number of earlier claims, income in the first month of earlier claims 1..4, domestic violence, first joint claim, my surplus alone, partner surplus alone, single claim after a joint one, apportioned, portion
-- relevant threshold = 2,000 + 300 = 2,300; the excess 2,500 - 2,300 = 200 is the original surplus
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2500 2000 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 200
-- second claim: 200 + 2,400 = 2,600 exceeds 2,300 by 300
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2500 2000 1 2400 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 300
-- second claim with no earnings in the first claim: 200 does not exceed 2,300
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2500 2000 1 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- a recent victim of domestic violence: no surplus counted
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2500 2000 0 0 0 0 0 TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- income of 2,300 does not exceed the relevant threshold 2,300: reg 54A does not apply
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2300 2000 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- the old award ended more than 6 months before 1 July 2026 (the 6 months run to 30 June): reg 54A does not apply
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2500 2000 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- entitled to universal credit since the old award ended: reg 54A does not apply
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE 2500 2000 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- first joint claim by two who each had an award: 120 + 80 aggregated
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2500 2000 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE TRUE 120 80 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 200
-- single claim after a joint claim: the Secretary of State apportions 90
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2500 2000 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE TRUE 90 EQUALS JUST 90
-- NOT COVERED: apportionment is in the manner the Secretary of State determines and none has been stated
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2500 2000 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- NOT COVERED: the text provides surplus earnings only to the fifth claim (four earlier claims)
#ASSERT `How much surplus earnings from my earlier award are treated as my earned income` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE 2500 2000 5 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- reg 55(4): the statutory payments that count as employed earnings.
#ASSERT `Is a payment of this benefit treated as my employed earnings` `statutory sick pay`
#ASSERT `Is a payment of this benefit treated as my employed earnings` `statutory neonatal care pay`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a payment of this benefit treated as my employed earnings` `personal independence payment`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a payment of this benefit treated as my employed earnings` `carer's allowance`)
-- reg 55: args = general earnings, of which benefits code, of which exempt, of which allowed expenses, of which service-user expenses, 7 service-user facts, statutory payment kind, its amount, repayment, repayment relates to paid work, repayment is self-employed earnings, pension contributions, income tax and NI paid, payroll giving
-- plain pay
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings for an assessment period` 2000 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `statutory sick pay` 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS 2000
-- 3,000 - 500 - 200 = 2,300; less 100 allowed expenses = 2,200; plus 120 sick pay = 2,320; less 150 + 300 + 10 = 1,860
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings for an assessment period` 3000 500 200 100 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `statutory sick pay` 120 0 FALSE FALSE 150 300 10 EQUALS 1860
-- the same as a service user: the 50 service-user expenses are also disregarded
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings for an assessment period` 3000 500 200 100 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `statutory sick pay` 120 0 FALSE FALSE 150 300 10 EQUALS 1810
-- a 400 tax repayment for paid work counts
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings for an assessment period` 2000 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `statutory sick pay` 0 400 TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS 2400
-- counted as self-employed earnings instead
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings for an assessment period` 2000 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `statutory sick pay` 0 400 TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 EQUALS 2000
-- personal independence payment is not one of the benefits treated as employed earnings
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings for an assessment period` 2000 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `personal independence payment` 500 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `What employed earnings am I treated as having if I am on strike` TRUE TRUE FALSE 2000 0 EQUALS 2000
-- contract terminated: what you have
#ASSERT `What employed earnings am I treated as having if I am on strike` TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 0 EQUALS 0
-- not withdrawn labour
#ASSERT `What employed earnings am I treated as having if I am on strike` TRUE FALSE FALSE 2000 800 EQUALS 800
-- no employed earnings before
#ASSERT `What employed earnings am I treated as having if I am on strike` FALSE TRUE FALSE 2000 0 EQUALS 0
-- reg 57: args = receipts, in kind, refund, allowed expenses, partnership, my share, paid HMRC, pension contributions, already deducted, unused losses
-- receipts 3,000 + 200 + 100 = 3,300; less 800 = 2,500; less 300 to HMRC = 2,200
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for an assessment period` 3000 200 100 800 FALSE 0 300 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 2200
-- half of 2,500 = 1,250; less 300 = 950
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for an assessment period` 3000 200 100 800 TRUE 0.5 300 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 950
-- a loss: nil self-employed earnings
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for an assessment period` 500 0 0 900 FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 0
-- less 100 pension contributions
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for an assessment period` 3000 200 100 800 FALSE 0 300 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS 2100
-- pension contributions already deducted from employed earnings
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for an assessment period` 3000 200 100 800 FALSE 0 300 100 TRUE 0 EQUALS 2200
-- less 1,000 unused losses
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for an assessment period` 3000 200 100 800 FALSE 0 300 0 FALSE 1000 EQUALS 1200
-- losses larger than the profit
#ASSERT `What are my self-employed earnings for an assessment period` 3000 200 100 800 FALSE 0 300 0 FALSE 3000 EQUALS 0
-- reg 57(5): args = cost deducted before, sold, stopped using, proceeds, market value
-- sold: the proceeds
#ASSERT `What am I treated as receiving for a business asset I sold or stopped using` TRUE TRUE FALSE 500 900 EQUALS 500
-- no longer used: the market value
#ASSERT `What am I treated as receiving for a business asset I sold or stopped using` TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 900 EQUALS 900
-- the purchase was not deducted
#ASSERT `What am I treated as receiving for a business asset I sold or stopped using` FALSE TRUE FALSE 500 900 EQUALS 0
-- neither sold nor given up
#ASSERT `What am I treated as receiving for a business asset I sold or stopped using` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 900 EQUALS 0
-- steps 1 to 3 give minus 400: a loss of 400
#ASSERT `What loss do I have for the assessment period` 500 0 0 900 FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 400
-- no loss
#ASSERT `What loss do I have for the assessment period` 3000 200 100 800 FALSE 0 300 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS 0
-- reg 57A(3): the last day of the old award must fall within the 6 months before the new one.
-- within 6 months (to 30 September)
#ASSERT `Do my earlier assessment periods count under my new award` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 8 15) TRUE TRUE
-- more than 6 months
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my earlier assessment periods count under my new award` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 10 15) TRUE TRUE)
-- information not provided
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my earlier assessment periods count under my new award` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 8 15) FALSE TRUE)
-- the Secretary of State does not treat them so
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my earlier assessment periods count under my new award` (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 8 15) TRUE FALSE)
-- the previous award did not end before the new one began
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my earlier assessment periods count under my new award` (YMD 2026 8 15) (YMD 2026 8 15) TRUE TRUE)
-- reg 58: args = kind, amount, wholly and exclusively, more than one purpose, proportion identifiable, proportion, unreasonable, flat-rate instead
#ASSERT `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` `an ordinary payment for the trade, profession or vocation` 200 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 200
-- a quarter of 200
#ASSERT `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` `an ordinary payment for the trade, profession or vocation` 200 FALSE TRUE TRUE 0.25 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 50
-- no identifiable proportion
#ASSERT `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` `an ordinary payment for the trade, profession or vocation` 200 FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- incurred unreasonably
#ASSERT `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` `an ordinary payment for the trade, profession or vocation` 200 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- interest may not exceed 41 pounds
#ASSERT `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` `a payment of interest in relation to a loan taken out for the purposes of the trade, profession or vocation` 300 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 41
#ASSERT `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` `expenses for business entertainment` 300 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- a car: only the mileage deduction
#ASSERT `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` `acquisition or use of a car` 300 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- a van, no flat rate taken
#ASSERT `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` `acquisition or use of a motor vehicle that is not a car` 300 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 300
-- a van, flat rate taken instead
#ASSERT `How much of a payment I made for my business can I deduct` `acquisition or use of a motor vehicle that is not a car` 300 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- 833 x 0.45 = 374.85, plus 167 x 0.25 = 41.75: 416.60
#ASSERT `What deduction can I take for the miles I travelled for my business` 1000 0 EQUALS 416.6
-- 100 x 0.24
#ASSERT `What deduction can I take for the miles I travelled for my business` 0 100 EQUALS 24
-- under 25 hours: nothing
#ASSERT `What deduction can I take for working from my home` 24 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What deduction can I take for working from my home` 25 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `What deduction can I take for working from my home` 50 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `What deduction can I take for working from my home` 51 EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `What deduction can I take for working from my home` 101 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `By how much is my deduction reduced because others live in my business premises` 1 EQUALS 350
#ASSERT `By how much is my deduction reduced because others live in my business premises` 2 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `By how much is my deduction reduced because others live in my business premises` 3 EQUALS 650
#ASSERT `By how much is my deduction reduced because others live in my business premises` 0 EQUALS 0
-- reg 60(1), (2): deprivation of earned income. args = amount, deprived myself, employer arranged it, to get universal credit, more universal credit resulted, the Secretary of State thinks that was foreseeable and intended
-- deprived myself to get universal credit
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having earned income that I was deprived of` 1000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1000
-- my employer arranged it
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having earned income that I was deprived of` 1000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1000
-- reg 60(2): the purpose is treated as existing
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having earned income that I was deprived of` 1000 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 1000
-- higher entitlement resulted but the Secretary of State does not think it was foreseeable and intended
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having earned income that I was deprived of` 1000 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- no higher entitlement resulted
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having earned income that I was deprived of` 1000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- not deprived
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having earned income that I was deprived of` 1000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- reg 60(3), (4): args = paid, comparable, could afford, reasonable pay, charity, SoS thinks free or cheap reasonable, approved programme, 7 service-user facts
-- paid nothing and the other person could afford 250
#ASSERT `What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide` 0 300 TRUE 250 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 250
-- paid less than comparable services
#ASSERT `What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide` 100 300 TRUE 250 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 250
-- NOT COVERED: paid the same as comparable services, so reg 60(3) does not apply and there is no treated payment
#ASSERT `What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide` 300 300 TRUE 250 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the other person could not afford more: reg 60(3) does not apply
#ASSERT `What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide` 0 300 FALSE 250 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a charity and the Secretary of State is satisfied: reg 60(4)(a)
#ASSERT `What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide` 0 300 TRUE 250 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a charity but the Secretary of State is not satisfied
#ASSERT `What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide` 0 300 TRUE 250 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 250
-- part of an approved programme: reg 60(4)(c)
#ASSERT `What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide` 0 300 TRUE 250 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- participating as a service user: reg 60(4)(b)
#ASSERT `What payment am I treated as having received for services I provide` 0 300 TRUE 250 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- reg 61(1): who must give information. args = the Secretary of State asks me, the income is from a Real Time Information employer
#ASSERT `Must I give the Secretary of State information to work out my earned income` TRUE FALSE
-- reg 61(2) applies: the Secretary of State relies on HMRC
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I give the Secretary of State information to work out my earned income` TRUE TRUE)
-- only when the Secretary of State requires it
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I give the Secretary of State information to work out my earned income` FALSE FALSE)
-- reg 61(2), (3): args = RTI employer, unlikely to report well, a reported payment looks wrong, nothing came from HMRC and that looks like a failure
#ASSERT `Are my employed earnings from this job based on what my employer reports to HMRC` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- exception (3)(a)
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my employed earnings from this job based on what my employer reports to HMRC` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- exception (3)(b)
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my employed earnings from this job based on what my employer reports to HMRC` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- exception (3)(c)
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my employed earnings from this job based on what my employer reports to HMRC` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- not a Real Time Information employer
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my employed earnings from this job based on what my employer reports to HMRC` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- reg 61(2) and (4): args = RTI employer, 3 exceptions, HMRC has told the SoS, amount reported, amount under reg 55
-- based on what was reported
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings from this job for the assessment period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1200 1500 EQUALS 1200
-- reg 61(2)(b): nothing received from HMRC means nil
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings from this job for the assessment period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 1500 EQUALS 0
-- exception: reg 55 amount
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings from this job for the assessment period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1200 1500 EQUALS 1500
-- not a Real Time Information employer: reg 55 amount
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings from this job for the assessment period` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 1500 EQUALS 1500
-- reg 61(5): the answer is the first day of the period. args = reported late, SoS decided it counts when received, first and last day when reported, first and last day when received
-- received in April, reported in May: the Secretary of State has decided April
#ASSERT `In which assessment period is my late or misplaced payment counted` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 4 1) (YMD 2026 4 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1
-- no determination: the period in which it was reported
#ASSERT `In which assessment period is my late or misplaced payment counted` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 4 1) (YMD 2026 4 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
-- not reported late: the period reported
#ASSERT `In which assessment period is my late or misplaced payment counted` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 4 1) (YMD 2026 4 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
-- reg 61(6): args = paid regularly each month, two payments in one period, SoS moved one, first and last day reported, first and last day of the other period
-- moved to June
#ASSERT `In which assessment period is one of two payments reported together counted` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
-- not moved
#ASSERT `In which assessment period is one of two payments reported together counted` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
-- not paid monthly: the power does not arise
#ASSERT `In which assessment period is one of two payments reported together counted` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
-- only one payment reported in the period
#ASSERT `In which assessment period is one of two payments reported together counted` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
-- reg 61(7): args = before adjustment, SoS made a determination, the adjustment
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings after the Secretary of State adjusts them` 1500 TRUE 200 EQUALS 1700
-- no determination: no adjustment
#ASSERT `What are my employed earnings after the Secretary of State adjusts them` 1500 FALSE 200 EQUALS 1500
-- reg 62: args = gainful, group, basis, own earned income, partner income, individual threshold, couple threshold, tax deduction from individual, tax deduction from couple, surplus, ap first, ap last, start-up?, su first, su last
-- net individual threshold 1,200 - 200 = 1,000 exceeds earned income 500
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 1000
-- earned income above the net threshold: what is earned
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 1500 0 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 1500
-- earned income equal to the threshold: not less than
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 1000 0 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 1000
-- not in the all-requirements group: reg 62 does not apply
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to no work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 500
-- not in gainful self-employment: reg 62 does not apply
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` FALSE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 500
-- joint: net couple threshold 1,500; 500 + 200 is below it; 1,000 - ((1,000 + 200) - 1,500 -> max 0) = 1,000
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `joint claimants` 500 200 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 1000
-- joint: 1,000 + 800 = 1,800 exceeds 1,500 by 300, so 1,000 - 300 = 700
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `joint claimants` 500 800 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 700
-- joint: combined 1,600 is not less than 1,500: what is earned
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `joint claimants` 500 1100 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 500
-- surplus earnings of 100 added: 600 is still under 1,000
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 1200 1800 200 300 100 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 1000
-- surplus earnings of 100 added: 1,050 exceeds 1,000: what is earned plus the surplus
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 950 0 1200 1800 200 300 100 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 1050
-- the whole assessment period is in a start-up period: reg 62(5) switches the floor off
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2027 5 31) EQUALS 500
-- the period begins before, ends within: touches the start-up period
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2027 6 14) EQUALS 500
-- the start-up period ended before the assessment period: the floor applies
#ASSERT `How much earned income am I treated as having under the minimum income floor` TRUE `subject to all work-related requirements` `a single claimant` 500 0 1200 1800 200 300 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS 1000
